ation Programming Interface","APSD":"Auto-Power Spectral Density","CCLD":"Constant Current Line Drive","COLA":"Constant Overlap and Add","CPSD":"Cross-Power Spectral Density","DTF":"Digital Tracking Filter","FEM":"Finite Element Model","FFT":"Fast Fourier Transform","FRF":"Frequency Response Function","GUI":"Graphical User Interface","ICP":"Integrated Circuit Piezoelectric","IDE":"Integrated Development Environment","IEPE":"Integrated Electronics PiezoElectric","IFFT":"Inverse Fast Fourier Transform","IP":"Internet Protocol","JSON":"Javascript Object Notation","MIMO":"Multiple Input, Multiple Output","PyPI":"Python Package Index","ReST":"Representational State Transfer","RMS":"Root-Mean-Square","SDS":"Sum of Decayed Sines","SRS":"Shock Response Spectrum","SVD":"Singular Value Decomposition","TRAC":"Time Response Assurance Criterion","UI":"User Interface","VK":"Vold-Kalman (Filter)"},"title":"Rattlesnake Vibration Controller","description":"User's Manual and Examples for the Rattlesnake Vibration Controller","thumbnail":"/Rattlesnake_Logo_Ban-9311d47f11b9c0b30a3123732ac40963.png","github":"https://github.com/sandialabs/rattlesnake-vibration-controller","keywords":["mimo","vibration","modal","structural-dynamics"],"parts":{"abstract":{"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","data":{"part":"abstract"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rattlesnake is a combined-environments, multiple input/multiple output control system for\ndynamic excitation of structures under test.  It provides capabilities to control multiple\nresponses on the part using multiple exciters using various control strategies.  Rattlesnake\nis written in the Python programming language to facilitate multiple input/multiple output\nvibration research by allowing users to prescribe custom control laws to the controller.\nRattlesnake can target multiple hardware devices, or even perform synthetic control to simulate\na test virtually.  Rattlesnake has been used to execute control problems with up to 200\nresponse channels and 24 shaker drives.  This document describes the functionality,\narchitecture, and usage of the Rattlesnake controller to perform combined environments testing.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"Wt4am3jvre"}],"key":"TIJKuPp0FN"}],"key":"uHK5ArASES"}],"key":"ZcJcK6w0iK"},"frontmatter":{"github":"https://github.com/sandialabs/rattlesnake-vibration-controller","numbering":{"heading_1":{"enabled":true,"continue":false},"heading_2":{"enabled":true,"template":"Chapter %s"},"figure":{"enabled":true,"continue":false},"table":{"enabled":true,"continue":false},"equation":{"enabled":true,"continue":false},"heading_3":{"enabled":true},"heading_4":{"enabled":true},"heading_5":{"enabled":true},"heading_6":{"enabled":true}},"keywords":["mimo","vibration","modal","structural-dynamics"],"abbreviations":{"6DoF":"Six Degree-of-Freedom","API":"Application Programming Interface","APSD":"Auto-Power Spectral Density","CCLD":"Constant Current Line Drive","COLA":"Constant Overlap and Add","CPSD":"Cross-Power Spectral Density","DTF":"Digital Tracking Filter","FEM":"Finite Element Model","FFT":"Fast Fourier Transform","FRF":"Frequency Response Function","GUI":"Graphical User Interface","ICP":"Integrated Circuit Piezoelectric","IDE":"Integrated Development Environment","IEPE":"Integrated Electronics PiezoElectric","IFFT":"Inverse Fast Fourier Transform","IP":"Internet Protocol","JSON":"Javascript Object Notation","MIMO":"Multiple Input, Multiple Output","PyPI":"Python Package Index","ReST":"Representational State Transfer","RMS":"Root-Mean-Square","SDS":"Sum of Decayed Sines","SRS":"Shock Response Spectrum","SVD":"Singular Value Decomposition","TRAC":"Time Response Assurance Criterion","UI":"User Interface","VK":"Vold-Kalman (Filter)"},"source_url":"https://github.com/sandialabs/rattlesnake-vibration-controller/blob/